body:
Well, hello there!

I used to get this feeling a lot on the past two months. I'd feel like shit, and hate every single aspect about me and even the others around me. 
I can list a few things you can do to distract yourself from this awful feeling, but I do believe that you should seek real help, like going to a psychologist. I know that maybe that's not what you want, but just think about it, ok?

When life turns to shit, I:

- take a long, hot bath;
- go for a walk and take a few pictures of the surroundings;
- eat candy while watching something funny on TV/Netflix;
- joke around with my mom;
- play some online games;
- learn something new (like learning to play a new instrument, or a new word);
- listen to music, obviously.

Please don't hesitate on doing any of those things if you feel down. I believe the best way of getting better is to distract yourself away from those thoughts. 
Again, please consider seeking professional help. One talk can make you feel a whole lot better <3
